y}{\\text{d}u}={e}^{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-5.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{u}\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =-5{e}^{u} \\\\  & =-5{e}^{4-5x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the sum rule of differentiation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{5}-{e}^{4-5x}) \\\\  & =5{x}^{4}-(-5{e}^{4-5x}) \\\\  & =5({x}^{4}+{e}^{4-5x}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546034 1080 "y=30 e x + 1 + 5 e" 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546034 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546034 1083 #uuid "3bfaf069-a4d6-5131-a87d-a208594f2c61" 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546035 1080 "y=- 12 e x - 4 e - 3" 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546035 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546035 1083 #uuid "4401eafb-fa33-5c95-b049-85b630f2f47d" 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546036 1075 #edb/ref 17592186546032 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546036 1075 #edb/ref 17592186546034 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546036 1075 #edb/ref 17592186546043 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546036 1075 #edb/ref 17592186546045 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546036 1075 #edb/ref 17592186546077 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546036 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546036 1077 "selection" 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546036 1078 #edb/ref 17592186546077 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546036 1079 #uuid "4506d1a2-b6f8-5a68-becb-87dba57a7620" 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546037 1068 #edb/ref 17592186546023 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546037 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546037 1071 "Calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$ if $f(x)=2x+{e}^{4x-6}.$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546037 1072 #uuid "46c70445-c7fa-5e96-b9db-24423c65d9d2" 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546037 1074 "First, we express $y={e}^{4x-6}$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny={e}^{u},\\,u=4x-6.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}={e}^{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{u}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =4{e}^{u} \\\\  & =4{e}^{4x-6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the sum rule of differentiation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x+{e}^{4x-6}) \\\\  & =2+4{e}^{4x-6} \\\\  & =4{e}^{4x-6}+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546038 1080 "\\left(4 x + 7\\right) e^{4 x + 7}" 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546038 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546038 1083 #uuid "4f3504cb-45f2-555b-80a1-81a0a0f42939" 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546039 1068 #edb/ref 17592186546076 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546039 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546039 1071 "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $y=3{e}^{-4x-6}+6$ at the point where $x=- \\frac{7}{4}.$" 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546039 1072 #uuid "52a84e58-ee14-59cb-b2fc-5dc806f58a59" 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546039 1074 "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny=3{e}^{u}+6,\\,u=-4x-6.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=3{e}^{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-4.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =3{e}^{u}\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =-12{e}^{u} \\\\  & =-12{e}^{-4x-6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the slope of the tangent to the curve at $x=- \\frac{7}{4}$, we have to evaluate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{x=- \\frac{7}{4}} & =-12{e}^{-4x-6}{|}_{x=- \\frac{7}{4}} \\\\ & =-12{e}^{(-4)(- \\frac{7}{4})-6} \\\\ & =- 12 e.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, the $y$-value of the point on the curve where $x=x_1=- \\frac{7}{4}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y_1 & =(3{e}^{-4x-6}+6){|}_{x=- \\frac{7}{4}} \\\\ & =3{e}^{(-4)(- \\frac{7}{4})-6}+6 \\\\ & =6 + 3 e.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we find the equation of the tangent at that point:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-y_1 & =m(x-x_1) \\\\ y-(6 + 3 e) & =(- 12 e)(x-(- \\frac{7}{4})) \\\\ y-(6 + 3 e) & =- 12 e x-(21 e) \\\\ y & =- 12 e x - 18 e + 6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546040 1080 "4 x e^{4 x + 7}" 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546040 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546040 1083 #uuid "576283f7-d522-5cbc-8f21-65c4b15b8858" 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546041 1080 "e^{- 4 x}" 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546041 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546041 1083 #uuid "5c1ee9ed-13be-5d25-80da-1864c503d155" 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546042 1080 "y=- 12 e x - 18 e + 6" 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546042 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546042 1083 #uuid "631a33cb-a6bf-5512-a0f9-90d28f159483" 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546043 1080 "y=5 e \\left(x - \\frac{5}{6}\\right) + 1 + 5 e" 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546043 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546043 1083 #uuid "72048a0c-73ca-54b2-aa19-72248fb1e5b6" 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546044 1080 "5 x^{4} + 5 e^{4 - 5 x}" 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546044 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546044 1083 #uuid "7367a804-a6e2-5743-81c8-c134ab3e3d40" 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546045 1080 "y=30 e \\left(x - \\frac{5}{6}\\right) + 5 e" 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546045 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546045 1083 #uuid "750cf673-67dd-5803-97c5-520a46254372" 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546046 1080 "y=- 2 e \\left(x - 3\\right) - 2 e - 3" 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546046 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546046 1083 #uuid "7c3f86e4-f000-591a-af10-3b0f2e76f24a" 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546047 1068 #edb/ref 17592186546056 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546047 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546047 1071 "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $y=-2{e}^{-3x+2}+3$ at the point where $x=\\frac{1}{3}.$" 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546047 1072 #uuid "7fd12a30-30af-5a77-a4c8-bf313d7546d2" 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546047 1074 "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny=-2{e}^{u}+3,\\,u=-3x+2.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=-2{e}^{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-3.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =-2{e}^{u}\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =6{e}^{u} \\\\  & =6{e}^{-3x+2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the slope of the tangent to the curve at $x=\\frac{1}{3}$, we have to evaluate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{x=\\frac{1}{3}} & =6{e}^{-3x+2}{|}_{x=\\frac{1}{3}} \\\\ & =6{e}^{(-3)(\\frac{1}{3})+2} \\\\ & =6 e.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, the $y$-value of the point on the curve where $x=x_1=\\frac{1}{3}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y_1 & =(-2{e}^{-3x+2}+3){|}_{x=\\frac{1}{3}} \\\\ & =-2{e}^{(-3)(\\frac{1}{3})+2}+3 \\\\ & =3 - 2 e.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we find the equation of the tangent at that point:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-y_1 & =m(x-x_1) \\\\ y-(3 - 2 e) & =(6 e)(x-(\\frac{1}{3})) \\\\ y-(3 - 2 e) & =6 e x-(2 e) \\\\ y & =6 e x - 4 e + 3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546048 1080 "\\frac{e^{4 x + 7}}{4}" 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546048 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546048 1083 #uuid "8fe2cbd2-f59b-5b92-9bbb-c00d3642dbdd" 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546049 1080 "y=- 6 e \\left(x - \\frac{1}{3}\\right) - 2 e + 3" 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546049 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546049 1083 #uuid "9237bc66-6da2-5b5f-af2c-8e5ce3b5744d" 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546050 1080 "x e^{- 4 x}" 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546050 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546050 1083 #uuid "944f0d6a-3b60-545c-b2e8-97b3032ade29" 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546051 1080 "y=12 e \\left(x - 2\\right) - 4 e - 3" 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546051 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546051 1083 #uuid "97abff75-225b-5630-aa11-86faced36582" 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546052 1068 #edb/ref 17592186546030 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546052 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535942 17592186045443 true] [17592186546052 1071 "Given that $f(x) = e^{-4x}$, find $\\frac{df}{dx}$." 13194139535942 17592186045443